---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="The FinSight Doctrine - Institutional Standards" description="The immutable blueprint for all content, design, and engineering on FinSight INDIA.">
	
	<main class="min-h-screen bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900 pt-24 pb-16">
		<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
			
			<div class="mb-16 text-center">
				<div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-gold-500/10 border border-gold-500/20 text-gold-600 dark:text-gold-400 text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase mb-6">
					<svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 21V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v16m14 0h2m-2 0h-5m-9 0H3m2 0h5M9 7h1m-1 4h1m4-4h1m-1 4h1m-5 10v-5a1 1 0 011-1h2a1 1 0 011 1v5m-4 0h4"></path></svg>
					Institutional Memory
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight mb-6">
					The FinSight <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-gold-500 to-amber-600">Doctrine</span>
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
					The immutable blueprint and first principles governing all content, visual design, and engineering workflows on FinSight INDIA.
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Core Philosophy -->
			<div class="bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-12 shadow-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 mb-16 relative overflow-hidden">
				<div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-2 bg-gradient-to-r from-gold-400 via-amber-500 to-red-500"></div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-4">The Core Tension</h2>
				<blockquote class="text-3xl font-light text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-snug italic border-l-4 border-gold-500 pl-6 my-6">
					"Taxation is emotional before it is mathematical."
				</blockquote>
				<div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
					<p>
						When a citizen receives a tax notice, their first reaction isn't to look for a formula—it is a spike in cortisol, a fear of the state, and acute anxiety. The old era of tax portals ignored this human experience, offering sterile codes and clinical jargon. We do not. We acknowledge the visceral reality of finance.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="space-y-8">
				<!-- Standard 1: Illustrations -->
				<div class="group bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 hover:border-gold-500/50 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300">
					<div class="flex items-start gap-6">
						<div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-900/30 flex items-center justify-center text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
							<svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 16l4.586-4.586a2 2 0 012.828 0L16 16m-2-2l1.586-1.586a2 2 0 012.828 0L20 14m-6-6h.01M6 20h12a2 2 0 002-2V6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"></path></svg>
						</div>
						<div>
							<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">I. Illustration Standards</h3>
							<ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">The Anxiety-to-Relief Arc:</strong> <span>Every article is a psychological journey. We meet the reader at the peak of their Situational Anxiety (the Hook). As uncertainty dissolves, we conclude with Empowerment and Relief. Illustrations must mirror this exact emotional cadence.</span></li>
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">Organic Immersion:</strong> <span>Illustrations are not "inserted images." They are relatable, hand-drawn, minimalist line-art (Varsity-style) that seamlessly melds into the background without harsh borders, appearing sketched directly onto the page.</span></li>
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">Anchored in Humanity:</strong> <span>We do not illustrate abstract laws. We illustrate the human being staring at a 15-day countdown clock at 2 AM. Art must be outside the box and extremely value-adding.</span></li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Standard 2: Content -->
				<div class="group bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 hover:border-gold-500/50 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300">
					<div class="flex items-start gap-6">
						<div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-900/30 flex items-center justify-center text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">
							<svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M11 5H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v11a2 2 0 002 2h11a2 2 0 002-2v-5m-1.414-9.414a2 2 0 112.828 2.828L11.828 15H9v-2.828l8.586-8.586z"></path></svg>
						</div>
						<div>
							<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">II. Content Standards</h3>
							<ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">Audacious Prose:</strong> <span>The writing must be fresh, modern, and fearless. No robotic corporate speak. It should read like a high-stakes financial thriller or a declassified dossier.</span></li>
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">360° Edge Cases:</strong> <span>Leave no stone unturned. Anticipate the "What if?" scenarios. Topics that are dense must be treated at length without compromising on simplicity.</span></li>
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">No Assembly Line:</strong> <span>Every article has a distinct personality. We must develop 10 to 50 different writing styles. Avoid repetitive subheadings and predictable structures that scream "auto-generated."</span></li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Standard 3: TL;DR -->
				<div class="group bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 hover:border-gold-500/50 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300">
					<div class="flex items-start gap-6">
						<div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-900/30 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">
							<svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"></path></svg>
						</div>
						<div>
							<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">III. TL;DR Standards</h3>
							<ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">Memory Retention Reality:</strong> <span>We may read a 3000-word article, but we keep very little of it in our mindspace. The TL;DR must be what a reader absolutely retains after closing the tab.</span></li>
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">Simple Language:</strong> <span>Colloquial and stripped of jargon. Even the most complex ideas are stored in the human brain as simple phrases.</span></li>
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">First Principles Only:</strong> <span>Focus exclusively on the irreducible core truth of the topic.</span></li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Standard 4: Interactive Artifacts -->
				<div class="group bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 hover:border-gold-500/50 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300">
					<div class="flex items-start gap-6">
						<div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-orange-50 dark:bg-orange-900/30 flex items-center justify-center text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400">
							<svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 17v-2m3 2v-4m3 4v-6m2 10H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z"></path></svg>
						</div>
						<div>
							<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">IV. Interactive Artifact Standards</h3>
							<ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">Reduce Cognitive Load:</strong> <span>Formulas and numbers must be presented intuitively. If a person wants to dabble in raw formulas, they buy a textbook. We are the explainers.</span></li>
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">No Negative Nags:</strong> <span>Never welcome a user with a negativity alert (e.g., "lifestyle degradation warning") before they have even input their actual data.</span></li>
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">Hide the Inapplicable:</strong> <span>Do not display outputs or fields that are mathematically inapplicable to the user (e.g., showing Presumptive Profit on ₹80L revenue).</span></li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Standard 5: Search & Taxonomy -->
				<div class="group bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 hover:border-gold-500/50 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300">
					<div class="flex items-start gap-6">
						<div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-rose-50 dark:bg-rose-900/30 flex items-center justify-center text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400">
							<svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M21 21l-6-6m2-5a7 7 0 11-14 0 7 7 0 0114 0z"></path></svg>
						</div>
						<div>
							<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">V. Search & Taxonomy Standards</h3>
							<ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">Index by Symptom, Not Statute:</strong> <span>The Income Tax Department categorizes by Statute (e.g., Section 44ADA). The citizen searches by Symptom (e.g., "tax on freelance software income"). We index by Symptom to capture real-world friction.</span></li>
								<li class="flex gap-2"><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300">The Complexity Premium:</strong> <span>The highest value exists where the tax code is ambiguous. Do not waste space on low-value commodities ("What is the slab rate?"). Focus on high-value friction.</span></li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

			</div>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>
